ISO/IEC 22989
-------------

src/iso22989/schema/*.yaml, src/iso22989/datamodel/ and project/ model the
concepts of ISO/IEC 22989:2022, Information technology - Artificial
intelligence - Artificial intelligence concepts and terminology (first
edition, 2022-07). They are this project's own work, written in its own
words, and they cite the standard's clauses and terms by number only. They
are not endorsed by ISO or IEC.

The standard is copyright ISO and IEC, and this repository carries none of
its text: no definition, note or heading, copied or paraphrased. ISO offers
the standard free of charge from its Publicly Available Standards page, under
its Customer Licence Agreement. That agreement grants no right to reproduce,
adapt or distribute the text, and it restricts use of the text with AI tools,
so this repository's licence cannot grant any of that either. Obtain the
standard, and any licence to reuse its text, from ISO or your national
standards body.

What the repository carries is the structure of the concepts, and this
project's own words about them. Copyright protects the way a work expresses
an idea, not the idea. The project takes the stricter reading European law
allows, under which even a short extract can be protected when it shows its
author's own choices (Infopaq International, Case C-5/08, Court of Justice of
the European Union). So each description was written from what the concept
means, in one or two sentences, not by rewording a definition. A concept keeps
its own name where that name is the term, such as AI agent, since a term of
art is the word for the idea and not the standard's expression of it.

scripts/check_overlap.py lets a person who holds a copy test this: it reports
any run of four or more consecutive words the repository shares with that
copy. The copy stays outside the repository.

src/iso22989/schema/iso22989-overlay.template.yaml lists the schema's
elements with empty placeholders and holds no text of the standard. A
licence holder may fill a private copy of it, which .gitignore keeps out of
this repository; that copy must never be committed or distributed.

ISO Open Data
-------------

src/iso22989/schema/iso-open-data/iso_deliverables_metadata.jsonl holds ISO's
records of ISO/IEC 22989:2022, ISO/IEC 22989:2022/FDAmd 1 and ISO/IEC
22989:2022/CD Amd 2, taken on 2026-11-05 from
https://isopublicstorageprod.blob.core.windows.net/opendata/_latest/iso_deliverables_metadata/json/iso_deliverables_metadata.jsonl.
Each line is ISO's record as published, without its "scope" field.
scripts/check_upstream_release.py pins each line by its hash and compares it
with the live dataset.

